---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy — 531 Strength"
  description="531 Strength collects no personal data. All training data is stored locally on your device."
>
  <section class="policy">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy · Effective May 27, 2026</div>
      <h1>No data collected<span class="dot">.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        531 Strength is a local-first training tracker. Your data stays on your
        device. There are no accounts, no servers, and no analytics.
      </p>

      <div class="body">
        <section class="block">
          <h2>What we collect</h2>
          <p>Nothing. The app does not collect, transmit, or store any personal
          information on external servers. All training logs, settings, and
          program data live in a local database on your device only.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="block">
          <h2>Local storage only</h2>
          <p>Your training data — lifts, training maxes, set logs, PRs — is
          written to a SQLite database on your device. It never leaves your
          device. Uninstalling the app deletes all of it.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="block">
          <h2>No account required</h2>
          <p>There is no sign-in, no profile, and no account creation. The app
          works entirely offline. Your data is yours and only yours.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="block">
          <h2>Over-the-air updates</h2>
          <p>The app may receive over-the-air JavaScript updates via EAS Update
          (Expo Application Services). These update checks transmit your device's
          app version and platform — no personal information. You can disable
          network access for the app entirely in your device settings; the core
          training functionality works without it.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="block">
          <h2>Device permissions</h2>
          <p>The app requests two device permissions:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Haptic feedback</strong> — vibration on set completion
            and rest-timer cues. No data is transmitted.</li>
            <li><strong>Local notifications</strong> — optionally used to alert
            you when a rest period ends, so you can step away from the screen
            during rest. All notifications are scheduled locally on-device and
            never leave your device. You can deny this permission; the rest timer
            still works on screen.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="block">
          <h2>Third-party services</h2>
          <p>None. The app does not integrate with analytics platforms, crash
          reporters, advertising networks, or any external service that would
          receive your data.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="block">
          <h2>Source available</h2>
          <p>The complete source code is publicly available. You can inspect
          exactly what the app does with your data (nothing) at
          <a href="https://github.com/alexcheuk/proof-531" rel="noopener">github.com/alexcheuk/proof-531</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="block">
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>Questions about this policy? Email
          <a href="mailto:hi@531ledger.app">hi@531ledger.app</a> or
          <a href="https://github.com/alexcheuk/proof-531/issues" rel="noopener">open a GitHub issue</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <div class="footer-note">
          This policy applies to the 531 Strength iOS and Android apps and this
          website. The policy may be updated; the effective date at the top
          will reflect the most recent revision.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy {
    padding: var(--space-5xl) 0 var(--space-4xl);
  }

  .wrap {
    max-width: var(--content-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--gutter);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .dot {
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--ink-1);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .block h2 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-0);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .block p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-1);
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .footer-note {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    line-height: 1.6;
    padding-top: var(--space-xl);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
</style>
